{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185959-descriptions-of-mana","id":1185959,"title":"Descriptions of Mana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-14T08:17:55-08:00","id":1185959,"title":"Descriptions of Mana","content":"I'm very familiar with the explanation of mana being supernal energy leftover / leaking into the world, and the related descrption of Hallows being at the most recognizable, dominating parts of a landscape, where senses seem heightened and everything feels more &quot;real&quot;.<br /> But I'm wondering if anyone knows more passages about how mana and tass look and feel.<br /> <br /> There are related questionsto this, such as why Hallows form, how tass is different from equivalent objects, and how items / people witg mana put inside are changed, what harvesting mana feels like and what a mage's awareness of their own mana pool feels like.<br /> <br /> I have this idea that since it can be foind in the fallen world, it is meant to exist there as a mystical force (like the wyrd, pyros, and others), and I'm trying to work on my understanding of it without simply saying &quot;its supernal&quot;.<br /> There may not be anything to support this in published content... but I thought I'd ask the forums if they know anywhere I can look for some of these descriptions.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that Signs and Sorcery will have some of the best answers, but if there's any other stuff I can look at in the meantime, I'd appreciate advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 02-14-2018, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T10:15:59-08:00","id":1185993,"title":"","content":"What Mana and tass look like varies a great deal. Tass, particularly, since it's bound inside whatever object it's tied to.<br /> <br /> Mana, though, carries Resonances, so it looks and feels akin to whatever Resonance it carries. Mana might be an ambient feeling of rage and pure fury, if harvested from a Hallow on some ancient ritual battleground. It might appear, under Mage Sight, as a candle flame to an Obrimos, if it carries Resonances of enlightenment. <br /> <br /> I've got a Thyrsus for whom Mana's overriding sensation is a feeling of &quot;fullness&quot;, like when you've just eaten a solidly satisfying meal but not overeaten; where you can practically feel the life-giving nourishment within you, making you feel stronger and better and more sure. The absence of Mana feels like being hungry; a noticeable emptiness within yourself, left behind by your body trying to get something it craves. It's a quiet weakness that you only notice when it's there.<br /> <br /> Sadly, that's all the advice I really have; use what's best for your players and characters. Not terribly helpful but... Is what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T11:54:31-08:00","id":1186027,"title":"","content":"That helps somewhat, but one of the things I'm trying to sort out is the difference between mana, essence, and resonance. Obviously all of these ideas are closely entwined, but some kind of distinction exists.<br /> Mana picks up whatever resonance its near (including, as some passages in Tome of Mysteries imply, the mage's own nimbus), but resonance exists independently on mana - even concentrated sources like ley lines and nodes do not always corrospond to Hallows - and since mana can change the resonance it carries, it must also be discrete.<br /> So I guess one of the root questions I'm looking at (that probably doesn't have an answer) is how resonance &quot;looks&quot; different when its within mana as opposed to free in the environment. I feel like there's a &quot;glass cup / flavored beverage&quot; analogy...<br /> <br /> And just musing on this is starting to form ideas... I'll do a follow up post in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T15:21:27-08:00","id":1186093,"title":"","content":"A Resonance is the &quot;feel&quot; a place has; a description of all the qualities it emanates. A knife used to kill someone carries Resonances of Knife, Sharpness, Blood, Pain, Death, Murder, Anger, etc., all of which radiate from it like some kind of hateful alpha decay.<br /> <br /> Mana and Essence pick up Resonances, or, perhaps more accurately, are shaped by them; like running clay through a mold. The result is essentially something that radiates and carries that same flavour of Resonance in the same way the original radiating object itself does. Mana inscribed with the Resonance of Murder <i>feels</i> like holding that aforementioned knife. Mana is the very distilled atom of raw power, and, in the shape of a Resonance, it's that power given over to that nature. The Mana sits within your soul like an aggressive lump; begging to be used to kill.<br /> <br /> Essence is more like Resonance distilled down to itself; droplets of Resonance. It takes the form of whatever it resembles in some iconic way; that murderous Resonance producing Essence that looks like a perpetually fresh bloodstain. Give it long enough and that Essence - that concentrated Resonance - seeks itself; a face starts to push out from within the puddle, and a mote is born; sucking on Resonances like a larval cicada, and waiting for a chance to hatch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T17:04:53-08:00","id":1186128,"title":"","content":"Essence formation is described in Lore of the Forsaken, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1035174-essence-just-what-does-it-look-like-taste-like-feel-like?p=1035259#post1035259\">I posted some excerpts here</a>, perhaps also in Book of Spirits, but how mages perceive it is vastly different from how werewolves do (which is the perspective Lore of the Forsaken takes).<br /> <br /> I'd be very surprised if there wasn't already a book in first edition that explains the specifics of Mana. Resonance, in terms of Mage, seems to be a more or less new thing (at least Supernally) and would probably be expanded on in Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T23:20:17-08:00","id":1186191,"title":"","content":"@nofather: exactly; those kind of passages regarding mana were what I was hoping someone might point me to. I was familiar with how extensively werewolf got into similar topics. Tome of Myseries had some descriptions, but only in the context of how spellcasting felt; it didn't dive into mana itself...<br /> <br /> <br /> So the idea my earlier post sparked was that mana is a &quot;reinforcing&quot; substance: its primary effect is to attach itself to other phenomena (objects, resonance, spells), amplifying those things and removing impurities. When resonance passes through it, it takes that existing feeling and intensifies it; when it weaves into an object, it creates a platonic ideal of that thing; it bolsters the supernal symbols in spells, letting them manifest more fully without as much disruption from paradox.<br /> This still fits with it being &quot;supernal energy leaked into the fallen world&quot; as it bonds to the supernal symbols underlying phenomena and makes them more present, covering up the obfuscations of the fallen world (the lie, tbe abyss) - thereby making whatever its in seem &quot;more real&quot;. And it bridges the ideas of &quot;takes on the resonance it interacts with&quot; and &quot;makes stuff feel more real&quot; concepts I was trying to rectify. ...it doesn't help me understand /why/ Hallows form, I guess, but does point to why they're the most dominating feature of an area.<br /> <br /> I think this cuts to the heart of what I was trying to understand, without needing to answer all the surrounding questions. It makes sense to me, seems to fit with everything I've read in the books, and seems obvious in retrospect... What do other people think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 02-15-2018, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T03:18:08-08:00","id":1186225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185959-descriptions-of-mana?p=1186128#post1186128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be very surprised if there wasn't already a book in first edition that explains the specifics of Mana. Resonance, in terms of Mage, seems to be a more or less new thing (at least Supernally) and would probably be expanded on in Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance isn\u2019t new, that\u2019s what the Mage Sight spells in 1e revealed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T13:16:52-08:00","id":1186387,"title":"","content":"Does Mage Sight still reveal resonance that corresponds to the type of MS used? Like would Death Mage Sight reveal the murderous resonance of a knife used in several murders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}